BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The First Sunset Mid-Autumn Dance Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T160000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17861969@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Dance
DESCRIPTION:The First Sunset Mid-Autumn Dance Festival\n\nJoin San Francis
 co Youth Ballet and Sunset Choreographers for the inaugural Sunset Mid-Aut
 umn Dance Festival\, a one-time performance celebrating the emerging dance
  community of San Francisco's west side.\n\nThis 70-minute\, family-friend
 ly program brings together emerging Sunset-based choreographers\, professi
 onal Bay Area dance artists\, and talented young dancers from San Francisc
 o Youth Ballet Academy for an afternoon of classical and contemporary danc
 e.\n\nThe program features original works by Ria Fifield\, Tai Lum\, Eli S
 hi\, and Sophia West\, exploring themes including family\, ritual\, devoti
 on\, cultural tradition\, change\, and the stories passed between generati
 ons.\n\nPresented by San Francisco Youth Ballet and Sunset Choreographers.
 \n\nDate: Sunday\, October 4\, 2026\nTime: 2:00 PM\nLocation: CAIS Theater
 \, 3250 19th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94132\nLength: Approximately 70 minu
 tes\nAudience: Family-friendly\n\nTickets and additional information are a
 vailable through the San Francisco Youth Ballet website.\n\n$22-27.\n\nPre
 sented by San Francisco Youth Ballet Theatre\n\n$22-27.\nSan Francisco You
 th Ballet Theatre\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/the-fi
 rst-sunset-mid-autumn-dance-festival-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34517847/29db49ab-dc1d-421b-934b-f7ca2744abd6.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Chinese American International School\, 3250 19th Avenue\, San Fr
 ancisco\, CA\, 94132
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/the-first-sunset-mid-autumn-danc
 e-festival-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The History of Concrete
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T163000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17857062@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Following the finale of his acclaimed HBO series “How To wit
 h John Wilson”\, NYC documentarian John Wilson looks to the bedrock of h
 is beloved New York City for inspiration and structure. Concrete\, the wor
 ld's most widely used building material\, appears as an ever-present life 
 force\, and John sets out to make the definitive documentary on the matter
 . After attending a workshop on how to write and sell a Hallmark movie\, h
 e decides to use the industry-approved Hallmark formula to tell this seemi
 ngly drab story and increase his movie’s appeal. But his foundation soon
  begins to crumble—literally and figuratively—as he struggles to balan
 ce artistic freedom with the realities of the modern film industry.\n\nThi
 s film can be used with loyalty cards or our 2026 annual CinemaSFBay passe
 s\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/the-history-of-concret
 e-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34492576/3146c9c4-580a-42fd-91e9-05f00aa75ca7.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/the-history-of-concrete-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE MUSIC: Color Green
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17748467@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:(((folkYEAH!))) presents:\n\nColor Green\n\nFor the California
 -based quartet Color Green\, playing music together is all about stepping 
 into the unknown. “When we play live\, I don’t really know what’s go
 ing to happen\,” says Noah Kohll\, one of the band’s two guitarists an
 d four vocalists. “You really have no idea what you’re going to get wi
 th this band\, which keeps things fresh for us and maybe makes the live ex
 perience special.” In a very short time\, they have developed a word-of-
 mouth reputation as a dynamic and unpredictable live act\, grounding their
  cosmic jams in earthy melodies and drawing from ‘60s SoCal folk-r0ck\, 
 ‘70s classic rock\, ‘80s underground rock\, ‘90s psychedelic dance-r
 ock\, and any other sound that catches their ears.\n\nAdaptable onstage an
 d off\, Color Green has shared stages with a range of groups that reflect 
 both the sophistication and the wild malleability of their sound\, includi
 ng Fuzz\, Kikagaku Moyo\, Circles Around the Sun\, Hiss Golden Messenger\,
  and the Brian Jonestown Massacre. Yet\, because they see boundless possib
 ilities from one note to the next\, they anchor their music in the urgent 
 present rather than the distant past. Color Green can be a million differe
 nt bands without losing their essential hue.\n\nThey capture that wild\, m
 ercurial quality on Fool’s Parade\, a meditation on loss\, grief\, confu
 sion\, frustration\, and the clarity to which they all lead. The album has
  the dynamic of a tight live set\, full of ebbs and flows\, highs and lows
 \, quiet moments lik...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/
 live-music-color-green-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33981463/28bb2e60-3c94-494e-98d6-e17ad21c89e0.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/live-music-color-green-tickets
END:VEVENT
