DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17757747@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Co-presented by Frameline\n\nThe Bay Area premiere of a new do
 cumentary offering an intimate look at the life and career of Emmy and Ton
 y Award–winning performer Bea Arthur.\n\nThe film is built around a neve
 r‑before‑seen interview with Arthur\, paired with new conversations fr
 om colleagues and friends who worked alongside her throughout her remarkab
 le career. From her early days at The New School\, to her groundbreaking w
 ork in off‑Broadway\, Broadway\, cabaret\, and television\, the document
 ary traces Arthur’s evolution into one of entertainment’s most distinc
 tive voices.\n\nAudiences will revisit her iconic roles as Maude and Dorot
 hy Zbornak on The Golden Girls\, her Tony‑winning turn as Vera Charles i
 n Mame\, and her decades‑long advocacy for the LGBTQ+ community. The fil
 m reveals the Bea Arthur few ever saw: sharp\, compassionate\, fiercely in
 telligent\, and deeply committed to the causes she championed.\n\nA post s
 creening conversation with filmmaker and producer Dan Watt in person.\n\nT
 ickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19742?siteToken=52wkfz
 mjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/12/bea-
 arthur-the-documentary-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
