 aving established a template forthe giallo with The Girl Who Knew Too Much
 \, Mario Bava set about cementing its rules with Blood and Black Lace. In 
 doing so\, he created one of the most influential films ever made - an Ita
 lian classic that would spearhead the giallo genre\, provide a prototype f
 or the slasher movie\, and have a huge effect on filmmakers as diverse as 
